Original commit body from d7cbb14df83b1372b9e3b6275dcd4147663fa528:

INV-vakaf split ONE instance of this field's axis-mixing out to
``call_locality`` (``cross_file``, bash/objc) and left four. An AST inventory
of all 107 producer sites found them; each is a different axis wearing the
construct field's name.

RESOLUTION STATUS — ``remote_external`` (erlang) / ``application_external``
(haskell). Read the emit sites: each is the ``else`` branch of a resolver
lookup whose ``if`` branch emits the unsuffixed sibling. The AST shape is
IDENTICAL — ``mod:func(args)``, function application — and the suffix marks
only whether the callee was found. That is already recoverable from ``dst``:
the unresolved branch mints a synthetic external node id, the resolved branch
points at an in-repo symbol id. Redundant, so folded.

RESOLUTION MECHANISM — ``chained_return_type`` (go). Names HOW the receiver's
type was obtained (through a chained call's return type), not what the call
looks like. The construct is a method call; the mechanism moves to
``resolution_quality``, alongside 'recovery' / 'ambiguous' / 'type_inferred'.

STATED TWICE ON TWO AXES — ``interface_dispatch`` (go). The sharpest case. The
same ``Edge.create`` already passes ``evidence_type="interface_dispatch"``, a
registered inference pathway meaning "edge inferred from interface-method
dispatch resolution". Naming it again under ``call_construct`` said one thing
twice on two different axes rather than saying two things. The construct is
``method``. Behaviourally free: that evidence type has ``base_confidence=None``,
so the edge keeps its explicit 0.75 / 0.5, and ``disambiguation_fallback`` is
untouched.

NOTE this differs from the fold target originally filed on INV-tadup, which
proposed moving it to ``meta['mechanism']``. That would have relocated the
duplicate rather than removing it. The item is corrected in its thread.

GUARDED, WITH A POSITIVE CONTROL. A live-tree AST walk asserts no producer
emits any of the four. It is an AST walk and not a grep because a regex over
source also matches its own docstrings — and the comments this fold leaves
behind name every one of the folded values. The guard ships with a second test
pointing the same walk at ``method``, which the tree emits at dozens of sites:
an assertion over an empty search passes just as happily when the walk is
broken, so the control is what makes the guard evidence rather than decoration.

CONSUMERS: none. Every reader of ``call_construct`` tests it against the single
literal ``"method"``; none of the four folded values had a reader. One test
asserted ``remote_external`` (updated) and one test DOCSTRING described it in
prose (updated too — an unupdated docstring is how WI-diruk drifted within the
hour of being fixed).

